  simplex-noise                MIT

ATTRIBUTION IS REQUIRED BEFORE MERGING ANY PORTED CODE. `docs/REUSE-MAP.md`
identifies files in the Claude of Tanks reference repository as candidates for
porting (notably `src/sim/terrainMobility.ts` and `src/sim/consumables.ts`,
both MIT in that project). MIT permits reuse but requires that the copyright
and permission notice travel with the code. When a port lands, add an entry
here in this form:

  <path in this repo>
    Derived from <upstream path> in Claude of Tanks.
    Copyright (c) 2026 Kevin B. Liu. Licensed under the MIT License.
    <one line: ported verbatim / adapted / reimplemented from public interface>

A same-shape reimplementation written from a public interface is not a
derivative work and does not require an entry. A close port does. If you are
unsure which you wrote, assume it is a port and add the entry.

Nothing may be ported from that project's Reserved Content paths under any
circumstances — see the License note in `AGENTS.md` for the enumerated list.
